A||||4||Fiero_Freak||4 speed autos?||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero_Freak||10-29-2000||09:47 PM||||   What are the easiest to swap in with the 2.8's?   Or I'm thinking of doing the 3.4.  How much modification is needed? and if so would I be better off going with a 3.8? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-29-2000||10:10 PM||||No easy swap for a four speed auto in a 3.1, 3.2, 3.4 or 3.8.  All need modifications for axles, brackets and some need ecm changes.||||reg||3
Z||000002||87GTZ34||10-29-2000||10:27 PM||||Is anything easy on the Fiero?  I'm putting in a 3.4 DOHC and 4T60E now.  The trans isn't so bad as I am using the PCM from the '96 MC.  You can pick up Pontiac 6000 trans brackets (F/R) and engine to trans bracket(on the right axle side) and use the Fiero mounts.  You have to add a pair of slots on the cradle for the back mount 3/4" to the right about 3/4" long.  Lar is right about the axles and I haven't started on that yet.  TerryK has conquered it & I believe he found out that axles from a certain year Pontiac minivan worked as drop in. (Search the archives on that one).  I would recommend the 440-T4 as it doesn't need computer to shift.<BR>Good luck & keep us posted.<P>------------------<BR>87GTZ34<P>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 10-29-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||10-30-2000||01:17 AM||||Call CVUnlimited http:www.cvunlimited.com  I think...<P>Ask for 94 U-Van (Pontiac Transport with a 3800) axles but with 86 Fiero manual transmission outer CV's. I say 86, because it gives them something to look up in their book. <P>Also, 94 and up A-car axles (Ciera/Century/6000) seem to be the same. Just swap in the manual trans Fiero outer CV's. THe auto's won't work. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-30-2000||07:52 PM||||Terry, don't you mean inners? The outer, wheel end, of all fiero CV's is the same.||||reg||1
